Go.dot patch 0001 for Tracktion Engine: an auto-tempo clip may be resampled.

Every clip in a launcher slot is auto-tempo (Tracktion forces it), and
AudioClipBase::getActualTimeStretchMode hands any auto-tempo clip whose mode is
`disabled` the default time-stretcher. With no stretcher compiled in that default
is `disabled` too, and nothing happens; with one compiled in, every clip is
stretched - including those Go.dot wants resampled, which then stop being
bit-exact and cost a stretcher's CPU for nothing.

This adds EngineBehaviour::autoTempoClipsUseDefaultTimeStretcher(), true by
default so Tracktion behaves as it always has, and reads it there. Go.dot's
engine behaviour returns false: a cue in varispeed stays on the resampler, and a
cue in timestretch names its stretcher explicitly.

Written to be offered upstream. Each file it touches carries a notice that Go.dot
modified it (GPL-3, section 5(a)).

Applied by Go.dot's build, cmake/WfgTracktionPatches.cmake, in the order
patches/tracktion_engine/series gives; refreshed from the working tree with
scripts/te-patches.py refresh, which keeps this header. Against Tracktion Engine
13b5132 (2026-09-23). Namespace draft section 22.3, decision DQ.

diff --git a/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.cpp b/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.cpp
index 23657cac089..0e11cee73e4 100644
--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.cpp
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.cpp
@@ -666,7 +666,14 @@ TimeStretcher::Mode AudioClipBase::getActualTimeStretchMode() const noexcept
 {
     TimeStretcher::Mode ts = timeStretchMode;
 
-    if (ts == TimeStretcher::disabled && (getAutoPitch() || getAutoTempo() || getPitchChange() != 0.0f))
+    // MODIFIED BY GO.DOT (https://github.com/pob31/go.dot), 2026-09-28, by
+    // patches/tracktion_engine/0001-auto-tempo-clips-may-resample.patch: auto-tempo alone
+    // takes the default stretcher only when the engine's behaviour says so, so a disabled
+    // clip can be resampled (EngineBehaviour::autoTempoClipsUseDefaultTimeStretcher).
+    const auto autoTempoWantsStretcher = getAutoTempo()
+                                          && edit.engine.getEngineBehaviour().autoTempoClipsUseDefaultTimeStretcher();
+
+    if (ts == TimeStretcher::disabled && (getAutoPitch() || autoTempoWantsStretcher || getPitchChange() != 0.0f))
         ts = TimeStretcher::defaultMode;
 
     return ts;
diff --git a/modules/tracktion_engine/utilities/tracktion_EngineBehaviour.h b/modules/tracktion_engine/utilities/tracktion_EngineBehaviour.h
index a21ea9c0d8d..2cd688c1175 100644
--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/utilities/tracktion_EngineBehaviour.h
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/utilities/tracktion_EngineBehaviour.h
@@ -124,6 +124,17 @@ public:
     /// thread to reduce audio CPU use.
     virtual bool enableReadAheadForTimeStretchNodes()                               { return false; }
 
+    /// MODIFIED BY GO.DOT (https://github.com/pob31/go.dot), 2026-09-28, by
+    /// patches/tracktion_engine/0001-auto-tempo-clips-may-resample.patch, which Go.dot's
+    /// build applies to this Tracktion Engine checkout. This function is Go.dot's addition.
+    ///
+    /// Should an auto-tempo clip whose time-stretch mode is disabled be handed the default
+    /// time-stretcher anyway? True by default, which is what Tracktion has always done.
+    /// Returning false lets such a clip be resampled instead - its pitch moving with its
+    /// speed - so a host can choose varispeed or time-stretch per clip while a stretcher is
+    /// compiled in. Auto-pitch and a pitch change still take the default stretcher.
+    virtual bool autoTempoClipsUseDefaultTimeStretcher()                            { return true; }
+
